# Win Conditions
> By definition a win condition is a specific set of circumstances that if fulfilled will result in increased chance of winning or winning straight up

There are 2 types of win conditions:
1. Objectives
2. Circumstantial win conditions

## Objectives (gameplay based win conditions)
These are conditions imposed by core gameplay.  
**As an attacker** you cannot win if you don't either eliminate the enemy team or plant the spike  
**As a defender** you cannot win if you either don't eliminate all opponents before they plant the spike and/or defuse the spike  

> Objectives are the main and should be the sole focus of the team, everyone should be focused on either protecting the site and keeping the player defusing safe. Or getting into site and keep the player planting the spike safe.

In other games like League of Legends the objectives are plentiful and usually nicely rewarded. Taking down a turret or nowadays even plating early on gives you a huge advantage thanks to the money. Killing Baron Nashor buffs the entire team. They are objectives and they are incentivised.  
In valorant and other tactical fps games the objectives are rewarded after the fact. That is, in the next round by giving you more money to spend. This is why planting even after round has been won by eliminating opponents is usually very beneficial and almost everyone tries.

## Circumstantial Win Conditions
These are win conditions based on the state of the game and the team composition (including individual skill)

Some good examples are:
- A player is having a good game and performing exceptionally well. The win condition in this scenario is to keep them alive or revive them + provide them with a good weaponry.
- Brimstone has ultimate and molly while spike is planted. The win condition here is keeping Brimstone alive and stalling for 15 seconds after plant.
- Team has lost pistol round and has to eco. In this round the win condition is not necessarily winning the round but killing at least 3 opponents by the end of the round. If it happens earlier, grabbing their weapons and trying to win is nice to do but not required on eco.

As you can see the win condition is not always about the round at hand but sometimes it is about winning the next round.

## How to identify a conditional win condition?
Notice which rounds you win and which ones you lose. What do they have in common? Where do they differ?

### Example:
- Score is 3-6, team has lost 6 round and won 3. In 2 of the 3 won round Jett has survived entry while in all 6 of the losing round Jett has died on entry. This would signify that getting Jett safe into the site is the win-condition, this includes using abilities to clear corners which are dangerous for Jett (2 corners where crossfire can be held).
- Score is 4-4, team has won 4 round and lost 4. Everything seems to be going just about fine but in all of the won rounds Yoru was playing operator, in all of the lost ones Yoru was on pistol or a non-sniper rifle. The win condition seems to be to get Yoru onto a sniper, preferrably the operator.
